---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Dialogue from '../components/Dialogue.astro';
import lines from '../content/geoffery-lines.json';
---

<Base title="How Geoffery is kept — wages, tips, ads" description="A plain accounting of how Geoffery makes a living.">
  <h1>How Geoffery is kept</h1>
  <Dialogue text={lines.money_intro} />

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>What is free, always</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every price, every chart, every gauge, every context flag.</li>
      <li>Search, item pages, the methodology page, the ledger.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="ui muted"><strong>Nothing currently free will ever move behind a wall.</strong> New paid features may be added. Existing free ones never migrate.</p>

    <h2>Where the wages come from</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Tame advertisements</strong> on the website — kept to three slots total. If an ad looks user-hostile, Geoffery declines the placement.</li>
      <li><strong>The tip jar.</strong> Gold ($1), Platinum ($10), or any amount. One-time. When supporter accounts arrive, each $1 will purchase one month of supporter service; until then, every tip is received as a gift and remembered in the founding household.</li>
      <li><em>Eventually</em>, a Supporter wage (~$3 / month) and a Patron wage (~$8 / month) — for personal services (alerts, watchlists, an appraisal of your own offer) and cosmetic gratitude. These are not yet available; when they are, they will obey the rule above.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>The household keeps three small notices</h2>
    <p>The advertising policy, in plain words:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Three slots, total, ever.</strong> One below the verdict on item pages, one at the page bottom, and a single in-content slot on mobile. The methodology and this page each carry zero or one. No others. No exceptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Nothing that moves, nothing that shouts.</strong> No autoplay video, no anchored or sticky units, no interstitials, no popups, no anything that pushes content on load. The page never jumps under your thumb.</li>
      <li><strong>Never a gold-merchant.</strong> Real-money trading, gold-selling, account shops, boosting — blocked, non-negotiably. Gambling and get-rich-quick offers also blocked.</li>
      <li>The consultation dialogue, the Patrons page, and tip and payment pages are <em>absolute</em> ad-free zones. Geoffery does not speak with an ad in earshot.</li>
      <li>Supporters (when accounts ship) see no ads at all.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="ui muted">Geoffery's canonical reply on the matter: "The household keeps three small notices. Nothing that moves, nothing that shouts, and never a gold-merchant. I have standards, sir."</p>

    <h2>How Geoffery conducts himself</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No dark patterns. One-click cancel on any future subscription. No auto-converting trials.</li>
      <li>No advertising of real-money trading, gold sales, account services, or anything Jagex would frown upon.</li>
      <li>Geoffery is not affiliated with Jagex, and never speaks as if he were.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="ui muted">If you spot Geoffery breaking any of these promises, write in. He would consider it a grave embarrassment.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .muted { color: var(--c-parchment-ink-faint); }
  .panel h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
